                        "review": "I loved playing this back in the day but holy hell what a terrible experience in a multitude of ways\n\nexperience\n\nremember the game is on steam but never tried it here. oh cool there are achievements and point shop items, cards and all that. lets go download it.\n\nfirst problem - the size\n\n44+ gb for dungeon fighter online??????? this is not the size I remembered. I was hoping for no more than 10 gb or so being generous. my memory has it pegged around 3, no more than 5 but maybe I am wrong. ok whatever download. come back later 44+gb has downloaded and before I go to launch it I think, hey wouldn't it be neat if my old account was still around and I could just pickup where I left off? many attempts at many emails and none claim to have any association with neople or dungeon fighter online so I give up on that idea, the game is worth starting over and hey this time there are achievements to keep me going. I am already on the website trying to determine if I have an account still or not so I register one to my primary email and commence to launch the game, excited I've already done the grunt work of making yet another account in my life, the fun one with special characters required for the password. now lets decide what I noticed first here... I guess it was the additional download required for the launcher\n\nsecond problem - the launcher really really really sucks and this part has an A and B section for how bad it sucks\n\nA- launcher download system is terrible and ultimately doesn't download with an error\nok so the launcher has to download and update the game. thats fine you don't want to fuss with steam systems and just keep it to one unified launcher update system I get it. so the download is either slow or immense because it gives you almost no information besides how fast its going, which wasn't fast, but it would fluctuate making calculating how long this would take not really possible with no eta. based on the bar it would have taken more than 30 minutes to an hour to finish this download. whatever I am patient, before the spoiler alert-error that never lets the download finish happens-spoiler alert, lets get to part b\n\npart b- the completely $&%^$&^%# account system through the launcher. I assume theres SOME kind of workaround for this MASSIVE oversight but if you download the game via steam, your ONLY option in the launcher is to REGISTER A NEW ACCOUNT. i already used my primary email and yes I did login to other emails just to check if i had an account there but I will be damned if I register a second account, to a non primary email that you expect me to link my primary steam account to, simply out of policy you can get bent. ok so shortly after I realize how f'd this is and find no way to link my account I just made with my steam account I point this out in a support ticket and ask how to proceed which is an ongoing thing and maybe I will update this if there is a tidy resolution but lets get back to part a continued\n\npart a continued - the download just errors out\n\nso after you wait a while it just says something about not being able to load the download list? but there are two errors and the other one just says something along those lines I dunno its an absolute joke. why even use steam and why make the initial download MORE THAN FOURTY FOUR GIGABYTES if you need to patch the game anyways. probably because of the issues I mentioned where it barely functions at all.  I honestly don't know how people access this game to play it besides I dunno registering a new account every single time they redownload the game? however long that takes\n\n\n\nin the end so far this has been the biggest dumbest waste of time joke of a game experience and I never even got in the game. I try not to burn a game especially when its one I already like but when you mess up this bad you deserve everything coming your way\n\n\nOFFICIAL SUPPORT RESPONSE\n-------------------------------------------------\n\nUpon checking, we confirmed that your account is registered as a Neople account. Please be informed that Neople accounts and Steam accounts are registered separately, and currently, there is no available option to link an existing Neople account to a Steam account.\n \nFor clarification, the Neople Launcher provides login options through email and password or third-party accounts, such as Google and Facebook. On the other hand, when using the Steam Launcher, you are automatically logged in to the email address you used with verifying and registering through Steam's verification process in Steam DFO Launcher.\n \nWe understand your concerns regarding the login process and appreciate you sharing your feedback with us. We will forward your concerns to the appropriate team for further review. While we cannot guarantee any changes or specific outcomes, your feedback is valuable in helping us improve our services.\n\n---------------\n\nmy response - see you in hell",
